<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI lists Nov '96 busiest cargo airports.</title>
<headline>ACI lists Nov '96 busiest cargo airports.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The world's 20 busiest airports in terms of tonnage handled during Nov '96 compared to 12 months earlier as shown by Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) data are:</p>
<p>    1  (3)  Memphis		  167,015 tonnes	 (up 16.9</p>
<p>pct)</p>
<p>    2  (5)  Hong Kong		159,274 tonnes	 (up 14.9)</p>
<p>    3  (2)   Miami		   158,313 tonnes	 (up 10.7)</p>
<p>    4  (4)  Los Angeles	    155,062 tonnes	 (up 11.8)</p>
<p>    5  (1)  Tokyo-Narita	   152,461 tonnes	 (up  5.1)</p>
<p>    6  (6) New York		  150,663 tonnes	 (up  9.9)</p>
<p>    7  (7) Frankfurt		 136,125 tonnes	 (up  3.7)</p>
<p>    8 (10) Seoul		     128,266 tonnes	 (up 18.3)</p>
<p>    9  (9)  Chicago		  115,105 tonnes	 (up  5.2)</p>
<p>   10  (8) Louisville		113,591 tonnes     (down  1.5)</p>
<p>   11 (14) Anchorage		 111,433 tonnes	 (up 23.3)</p>
<p>   12 (11)  Singapore		110,511 tonnes	 (up 11.8)</p>
<p>   13 (13)  Amsterdam		106,356 tonnes	 (up  8.5)</p>
<p>   14 (12) London Heathrow	 102,852 tonnes	 (up  4.2)</p>
<p>   15 (16)  Paris-CDG		 89,295 tonnes	 (up 12.2)</p>
<p>   16 (15) New York Newark	  82,083 tonnes	 (up  2.7)</p>
<p>   17 (19) Taipei		     78,695 tonnes	 (up 20.9)</p>
<p>   18 (17)  Dallas Fort Worth     72,316 tonnes	 (up  4.3)</p>
<p>   19 (18)  Atlanta		   67,633 tonnes	 (up  3.6)</p>
<p>   20 (20)  San Francisco	   63,866 tonnes	 (up  8.2)</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
